From: DotRedstone <dotredstone@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: fix Xiaomi battery current
 direction

The Xiaomi SM8550 battery firmware reports positive current while the
battery is discharging and negative current while it is charging.  This
is opposite to the Linux power-supply ABI and makes UPower override a
correct Charging status with Discharging.

Invert CURRENT_NOW for the Xiaomi variant so desktop power indicators
and charge-rate calculations receive ABI-compliant values.

---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -561,6 +561,8 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_bat_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW:
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.current_now;
+		if (battmgr->variant == XIAOMI_BATTMGR_SM8550)
+			val->intval = -val->intval;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_POWER_NOW:
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.power_now;
--
2.50.1
